From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:02:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test_elf_module: the Switch test is skipped when the
 toolchain is absent

It ran without REMILL_BUILD and died with a TypeError instead of skipping, like the
other classes of the file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: A test that needs Remill must skip without it, so the Linux CI can run the engine tests without a toolchain
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#5

---
 dm/tools/tests/test_elf_module.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dm/tools/tests/test_elf_module.py b/dm/tools/tests/test_elf_module.py
index cb86da2..a04dbd8 100644
--- a/dm/tools/tests/test_elf_module.py
+++ b/dm/tools/tests/test_elf_module.py
@@ -220,6 +220,7 @@ class LoadingWithJit(unittest.TestCase):
         finally: d.cleanup()
 
 
+@unittest.skipUnless(READY, 'needs REMILL_BUILD, clang++, unicorn and capstone')
 class Switch(unittest.TestCase):
     def test_the_cases_of_a_switch_are_entries_and_a_dispatch_stays_in_the_recompiled_code(self):
         d, paths = make_dir(mf.module_d())
